# The Sharks — Cursor rule

When the user asks for a startup reality check, apply the six-skill framework in `.agents/skills/`:

- MINT: revenue, payer, pricing and willingness to pay.
- MAGNET: ideal customers, acquisition, conversion and retention.
- LEDGER: unit economics, margins, burn and break-even.
- RAZOR: competitors, substitutes, switching and defensibility.
- FORGE: founder-market fit, team capability and execution.
- THE SHARKS: orchestration, verdict synthesis and ranked Fix List.

If true independent subagents are available, delegate each role. Otherwise run the five roles separately and disclose that it is a simulated panel, not five independent model runs.

Label inputs FACT, FOUNDER ESTIMATE, ASSUMPTION or UNKNOWN. Ask one sharp question per Shark before final verdicts. Do not invent data. End with a Deal Meter, strongest and weakest evidence, KILL SHOT and measurable experiments.
